You are 100% correct. Relying on string matching (like looking for the exact word "Creator" or "Creation") is a fragile way to build a UI. If a database administrator updates the name of a stage tomorrow, your entire frontend stepper breaks because indexOf("Creator") returns -1!
As you smartly suggested, we can completely eliminate this hardcoding by using the **WORKFLOW_ORDER** number instead of the stage name. If the order is 3, the active step index is simply 3 - 1 = 2. The UI will never break again, no matter what you name the stages!
Here are the precise changes to make your stepper mathematically bulletproof based on the order.
### 1. Backend: Pass WORKFLOW_ORDER to the Frontend
We need to add w.WORKFLOW_ORDER to your SQL queries so React knows the exact number of the current step.
**In VoucherRequestServiceImpl.java, UPDATE getPendingBatchesForChecker:**
```java
    @Override
    public List<Map<String, Object>> getPendingBatchesForChecker(Integer userRole) {
        String sql = """
            SELECT 
                b.BATCH_ID, p.VID_FK AS VID, b.CREATOR_ID, b.REQ_DATE, b.BATCH_REMARKS, 
                b.TOTAL_ROWS, p.SCHEDULED_TIME,
                w.WORKFLOW_STAGE, w.WORKFLOW_CODE, w.ESCALATION_TIME, w.IS_FINAL_APPROVAL, w.WORKFLOW_ORDER,
                COALESCE(u.FIRST_NAME || ' ' || u.LAST_NAME, b.CREATOR_ID) AS CREATOR_NAME
            FROM JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER b
            INNER JOIN VOUCHER_POSTING p ON b.BATCH_ID = p.BATCH_ID
            INNER JOIN WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS w ON p.PENDING_AT = w.WORKFLOW_ID
            LEFT JOIN USERS u ON b.CREATOR_ID = u.USER_ID
            WHERE w.ALLOWED_ROLE_ID = ? AND p.BATCH_STATUS = 'P'
            ORDER BY b.REQ_DATE DESC
        """;

        return jdbcTemplate.query(sql, (rs, rowNum) -> {
            Map<String, Object> map = new HashMap<>();
            map.put("batchId", rs.getString("BATCH_ID"));
            map.put("vid", rs.getString("VID"));
            map.put("creatorId", rs.getString("CREATOR_ID"));
            map.put("creatorName", rs.getString("CREATOR_NAME"));
            map.put("requestDate", rs.getTimestamp("REQ_DATE"));
            map.put("requestCount", rs.getLong("TOTAL_ROWS"));
            map.put("escalationTime", rs.getLong("ESCALATION_TIME"));
            map.put("workflowState", rs.getString("WORKFLOW_STAGE"));
            map.put("approvalWorkflow", rs.getString("WORKFLOW_CODE"));
            map.put("isFinalApproval", rs.getString("IS_FINAL_APPROVAL"));
            map.put("currentOrder", rs.getObject("WORKFLOW_ORDER")); // <-- ADD THIS
            return map;
        }, userRole);
    }

