### Why this fixes the issue forever:
Because your backend API /JS/voucher/workflow/steps/{workflowCode} fetches the array of stages ordered perfectly by WORKFLOW_ORDER ASC, the React frontend array will *always* align with the WORKFLOW_ORDER numbers from the database.
If you rename "Creator" to "Creation" or "Initiator", the string doesn't matter anymore. React just says, *"The database says this batch is at Order 2, so I will highlight the 2nd circle in the stepper."* Perfectly dynamic!
